incident("AUTONOMY-CERT-IMPL") = {
  body: "rmw3 authorized (a): implement checks/autonomy-cert — the machine-verifiable drill that makes the autonomy guarantee (C1-C6) REAL, not a declaration. Previously the guarantee was design-only (proposal). Now it is an ACTION: a check that injects the exact fault for each criterion and asserts DETECTION.",
  root_cause: "Autonomy was a prose guarantee. To certify 'autonomy first' before vsf-rsi, the criterion set needed to be executable as negative-controls.",
  fix: "scripts/vsl/check_autonomy_cert.py + checks/autonomy-cert (R4.1 pass|fail). C1: injects each violation class (P4-ORPHAN/P4-DANGLING/P5-PLAN/P5-SPECSRC-MISSING/P6-ADVERSARIAL) into a sandbox, asserts the gate/hook catches it. C2: asserts every checks/* fail-mode discriminates (exit 1 on detection). C3: principle-gate-trace pass=0. C4: injects a 'stable' registry pkg with no artifact, asserts G3 flags P6-DANGLING-REGISTRY. C5: injects a malformed .vsm, asserts VSL-balance check catches it. C6: asserts scenario_memory_spec links the autonomy proposal and an IR cites it. While implementing, found + FIXED a real contract bug: plugins-port-verify fail-mode exited 0 on detection (inverse of R4.1); realigned to exit 1 (matches package-conformance-valid / child-boot-valid / principle-gate-traceable).",
  lesson: "Even the discipline checks must obey the discipline: a check's negative-control must use ONE convention (fail->exit 1 on detect). A check that exits 0 on detection is itself a silent gap (it would look 'green' while missing the fault). Consistency of the R4.1 contract across ALL checks is part of the autonomy guarantee.",
  references: ["scripts/vsl/check_autonomy_cert.py", "checks/autonomy-cert", "checks/plugins-port-verify", "docs/autonomy_guarantee_proposal.vsm"],
}
⟦ /autonomy_cert_impl ⟧
